%%^ carveFrontmatterFence

%% Frontmatter is a START-OF-FILE construct - its rule is anchored with `\%^` -
%% so it needs a file of its own to be asserted at all. It is here for a second
%% reason too: the three dashes are also a thematic break and the first two are
%% also the en-dash typography rule, and on a tie Vim gives the LAST-DEFINED
%% item priority. The frontmatter region used to be defined first and lost both
%% ties, so a document's own header was coloured as punctuation.

Body text.
%%^ (none)

